# 24. Searching for Text

Emacs provides an incremental search feature.

Shortcut:

```text
C-s
```

This means:

```text
Ctrl + s
```

After pressing `C-s`, type the text you want to find.

Example:

```text
C-s
```

Then type:

```text
Linux
```

Emacs searches for `Linux` while you type.

---

# 25. Searching Backward

Use:

```text
C-r
```

Meaning:

```text
Ctrl + r
```

This performs an incremental search backward.

### Example

If the buffer contains:

```text
Linux
Python
Linux Commands
Networking
Linux Security
```

Using:

```text
C-r
```

and searching for:

```text
Linux
```

moves backward through matching occurrences.

---

# 26. Real-World Search Example

