# 33. Cut and Copy Concepts in Emacs

Emacs uses the concepts:

```text
Kill
Yank
```

These are similar to:

```text
Cut
Paste
```

### Kill

Removing text and storing it for later use is called **killing**.

### Yank

Putting the killed text back is called **yanking**.

---

# 34. Kill a Line

Use:

```text
C-k
```

This kills text from the cursor position to the end of the line.

Example:

```text
Linux is a powerful operating system.
     ^
```

Press:

```text
C-k
```

The text after the cursor is removed.

---

# 35. Yank Text

Use:

```text
C-y
```

This yanks previously killed text back into the buffer.

This is similar to pasting.

---

# 36. Real-World Kill and Yank Example

Suppose you have:

```text
Name: Niranjan
Course: MCA
City: Bangalore
```

You want to move:

```text
Course: MCA
```

to another location.

You can kill the relevant text and then use:

```text
C-y
```

to insert it at the desired location.

---

# 37. Undo Changes

Use:

```text
C-x u
```

or:

```text
C-_
```

to undo changes.

The easiest command to remember is:

```text
C-x u
```

### Real-World Example

If you accidentally delete an important paragraph, use:

```text
C-x u
```

to undo the deletion.

---

# 38. Redo

Emacs can also redo changes through its undo system.

Repeated undo/redo operations allow you to move through previous editing states.

The exact behavior depends on the Emacs version and undo system, so the safest beginner approach is to use:

```text
C-x u
```

and understand Emacs's undo history.

---

# 39. Selecting Text

Emacs uses the concept of a **mark** to define a region.

Start a region with:

```text
C-Space
```

Then move the cursor.

The area between the mark and cursor becomes the selected region.

---

# 40. Kill Selected Text

After selecting a region, use:

```text
C-w
```

to kill the selected text.

This is similar to cutting selected text.

---

# 41. Copy Selected Text

After selecting a region, use:

```text
M-w
```

to copy the selected text.

Then use:

```text
C-y
```

to yank/paste it.

---

